<h1>Cut (Polygonal Area)</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>This command is accessible from <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Mesh &gt; Cut</b></span>.</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CDescription">
<p class="Description"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span></b> <span class="Command">Cut (Polygonal Area)</span> command deletes selected mesh triangles that fall into a drawn polygon or selected plane and generates a new hidden mesh entity from them.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span class="Command">Cut (Polygonal Area)</span> command is grayed if there is no selection or all selections are hidden. It works on wholly selected entities as well as on partial selections.</p>
<p>This commands works in two ways:</p>
<p>1. Interactively definition of polygon for cutting plane.</p>
<p class="whs4">When call <span class="Command">Cut (Polygonal Area)</span> KUBE will enter in drawing mode. The mouse pointer will become a scissors. Then use the left mouse button to draw a polygon on the mesh in the viewport. Hold down the <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Ctrl</b></span> key to draw line parallel to the viewport axes. When double-click, the polygon will be automatically closed and the triangles will be deleted. Although it is not recommended, you can rotate the viewport using <span class="Shortcut">Shift + left mouse button</span>, pan using <span class="Shortcut">Shift + right mouse button</span>, and zoom using <span class="Shortcut">Shift + middle mouse button</span> or the mouse wheel, while in this mode.</p>
<p class="whs4"><img src="../images/cut_polygonal_area_1.gif" width="21px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""> &#160;Mouse pointer in <span class="Mode">Cut (Polygonal Area)</span> mode.</p>
<p class="whs4"><span class="Mode">Cut (Polygonal Area)</span> mode will remain active until you close this mode.</p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Example</u></span></a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP164146659" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../images/cut_polygonal_area_2.gif" width="717px" height="415px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
<p>Mesh before polygon is closed</p>
<p>&#160;<img src="../images/cut_polygonal_area_3.gif" width="717px" height="415px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
<p>Mesh after polygon is closed</p>
<p>&#160;<img src="../images/cut_polygonal_area_4.gif" width="717px" height="415px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
<p>Mesh after polygon is closed with cut mesh unhidden</p>
</div>
<p>2. Selection of a datum entity that defines the cutting plane. Planes, circles, and cylinders are allowed for cutting.</p>
<p class="whs4"><img src="../images/cut_polygonal_area_0.gif" width="219px" height="220px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB">Listbox</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Select a datum entity from the list of visible planes, circles, and cylinders in the scene. In case of circle it is projected on the mesh surface. The other entities must intersect with the selection.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Tolerance</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Tolerance for defining borders of the cutting area. This parameter is applicable for circles and cylinders only. Default value is 0.01mm.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Apply</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">button</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Press this button to cut the mesh selection and to create the cut sub-mesh.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Examples</u></span></a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP165040417" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../images/cut_polygonal_area_example2.gif" width="645px" height="370px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></p>
<p>Mesh cut by a plane</p>
<p><img src="../images/cut_polygonal_area_example1.gif" width="493px" height="410px" border="0" class="img_whs9" alt=""></p>
<p>Mesh cut by circle and cylinder</p>
</div>
<p>If the cutting line passes over a triangle, it is divided in three new triangles  two from the original mesh and one from the cut mesh, or vice versa (depending on which side of the cutting line is inner).</p>
<p><img src="../images/cut_polygonal_area.gif" width="575px" height="237px" border="0" class="img_whs10" alt=""></p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="Use"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use:</b></span> <span class="Command">Cut Polygonal Area</span> to cut large meshes into sub-meshes.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>

